sdk/include/platform/sunburst/platform-simulation_exit.hh: print the exit code before the exit string

Local change (ibex_cheriot_verification). On Sonata (the sunburst platform) platform_simulation_exit()
ignores its code and always sends the same magic string, so a scheduler panic or
fail-simulator-on-error.h's exit(1) ends the run exactly like a clean exit(0) when the last thread
exits. This prints "Simulation exit code: <n>" first; ibex/dv/scripts/cheriot_rtos_results.py requires
code 0 for the runs that have no verdict lines of their own (regress-drs, regress-tei, hwrev-irq).
Applied to the cheriot-rtos submodule's working tree by the root Makefile (cheriot-rtos-patch),
idempotently; the submodule is ignore = dirty in .gitmodules.

--- a/sdk/include/platform/sunburst/platform-simulation_exit.hh
+++ b/sdk/include/platform/sunburst/platform-simulation_exit.hh
@@ -18,6 +18,27 @@
 #	else
 #		error No UART found in platform_simulation_exit
 #	endif
+	// Local change (ibex_cheriot_verification): print the exit code. The magic
+	// string below is the same for every code, so without this a scheduler
+	// panic or an error handler's exit(1) ends the run exactly like a clean
+	// exit(0).
+	const char *codeString = "Simulation exit code: ";
+	while (char ch = *codeString++)
+	{
+		uart->blocking_write(ch);
+	}
+	char digits[10];
+	int  digitCount = 0;
+	do
+	{
+		digits[digitCount++] = static_cast<char>('0' + code % 10);
+		code /= 10;
+	} while (code != 0);
+	while (digitCount > 0)
+	{
+		uart->blocking_write(digits[--digitCount]);
+	}
+	uart->blocking_write('\n');
